    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup for May 14 relies on **Will Smith** (64.10) to anchor our production against Landen Roupp. **Will Smith** remains our highest-scoring option, benefiting significantly from a projected #2 spot in the order and a favorable park environment that offsets the respectable xERA of the opposing starter. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** (60.25) stands out as a strong play; his ability to leverage a favorable ballpark and his refined position in the four-hole makes him our primary engine for counting stats today. While **Brendan Donovan** (59.46) sits just outside the 60+ \"Strong\" tier, he offers the most efficient platoon edge of the day against Burrows, utilizing a +14% dynamic platoon boost that makes him a must-start despite the neutral park factors.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with our exposure to Emmet Sheehan. Both **Luis Arraez** (46.02), **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.15), and **Matt Chapman** (43.58) draw difficult matchups against Sheehan\u2019s 3.16 xERA. **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Luis Arraez** receive minor boosts from their projected leadoff/two-hole status, but the elite SP skill of Sheehan creates a tangible ceiling risk across these slots. **Gavin Sheets** (41.47) rounds out the active roster, though his value is thinning against Harrison; he barely clears our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, primarily because we lack superior alternatives for the current slate.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Drew Gilbert** (36.02). He flirted with the lineup, but ultimately lacked the necessary projection floor due to an assumed #8 spot in the order, which aggressively suppressed his rating. **Wenceel Perez** (34.70) was similarly considered but suffered from a negative platoon dynamic against McLean, keeping him firmly on the bench. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Geraldo Perdomo** unavailable due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin to preserve game caps for higher-leverage matchups later in the week. We are monitoring the pending lineup statuses for **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert**; should these projections fluctuate, we will re-evaluate the risk to our batting average stability.",
